ay]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133154537.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-jazz-guitarist-pritesh-walia-detained-by-ice-claim-friends-and-family-phone-taken-away/articleshow/133154537.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-jazz-guitarist-pritesh-walia-detained-by-ice-claim-friends-and-family-phone-taken-away/articleshow/133154537.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-11T18:08:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133154742,imgsize-36314.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the day by Elon Musk: "When something is important enough, you do it even if the odds are not in your favor"]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133154014.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/quote-of-the-day-by-elon-musk-when-something-is-important-enough-you-do-it-even-if-the-odds-are-not-in-your-favor-a-lesson-on-conviction-risk-and-pursuing-goals-worth-the-uncertainty/articleshow/133154014.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/quote-of-the-day-by-elon-musk-when-something-is-important-enough-you-do-it-even-if-the-odds-are-not-in-your-favor-a-lesson-on-conviction-risk-and-pursuing-goals-worth-the-uncertainty/articleshow/133154014.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-11T17:57:51+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133154273,imgsize-76520.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Over 100,000 cuttlefish gather in Australia yearly; fewer than 10 arrived in 2026, baffling scientists]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133152398.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Giant Australian cuttlefish at Point Lowly faced a drastic population plunge in 2026, with researchers noting less than ten cuttlefish spotted per dive, a historic low. The downturn is potentially tied to an algal bloom in South Australia, which may have adversely affected the cuttlefish or diminished their food availability. Conservation initiatives and a tourism moratorium have been established to facilitate a revival of the cuttlefish numbers.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/every-winter-more-than-100000-cuttlefish-gather-in-australia-in-a-mating-period-that-is-the-only-one-in-the-world-but-in-2026-fewer-than-10-arrived-and-scientists-are-trying-to-figure-out-why/articleshow/133152398.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/every-winter-more-than-100000-cuttlefish-gather-in-australia-in-a-mating-period-that-is-the-only-one-in-the-world-but-in-2026-fewer-than-10-arrived-and-scientists-are-trying-to-figure-out-why/articleshow/133152398.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-11T18:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133152447,imgsize-178981.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Atlanta turned a 7,000-pound Colorado turbine blade into a 50-foot bridge at Beaverbrook Park]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133153113.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a remarkable display of innovation, a retired wind turbine blade has been repurposed into a pedestrian bridge at Beaverbrook Park in Atlanta. This 15-meter structure, weighing around 7,000 pounds, was transported from Colorado and creatively adapted by researchers to fulfill the role of public infrastructure. This pioneering project marks the first instance of its kind in the United States, building upon the Re-Wind Network's prior endeavors.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/atlanta-reused-a-nearly-7000-pound-wind-turbine-blade-as-a-50-foot-pedestrian-bridge-the-retired-colorado-blade-now-carries-walkers-through-beaverbrook-park/articleshow/133153113.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/atlanta-reused-a-nearly-7000-pound-wind-turbine-blade-as-a-50-foot-pedestrian-bridge-the-retired-colorado-blade-now-carries-walkers-through-beaverbrook-park/articleshow/133153113.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-11T17:21:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133153319,imgsize-178196.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Why is Chud The Builder finally out of jail after two months? Here’s what we know]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133147934.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Dalton Eatherly, known as Chud The Builder, has been released from jail after two months. He posted a $1 million bond, securing his freedom from Montgomery County Jail. Eatherly faces attempted murder charges linked to a May courthouse shooting incident. He is also involved in a separate Davidson County case for alleged restaurant theft. Both cases are now proceeding to a grand jury for further review.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/why-is-chud-the-builder-finally-out-of-jail-after-two-months-heres-what-we-know/articleshow/133147934.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/why-is-chud-the-builder-finally-out-of-jail-after-two-months-heres-what-we-know/articleshow/133147934.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-11T16:05:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133148036,imgsize-453085.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Mahomes On Chiefs Ambassadors: QB welcomes returning stars as mentors; says it connects eras]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133146424.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Patrick Mahomes opened up about the emotional impact of seeing former Kansas City Chiefs teammates return to training camp through the team’s Ambassadors program. He recalled shared memories from demanding camps and praised the veterans for helping younger players understand the NFL grind. Mahomes especially highlighted Tyrann Mathieu’s leadership, preparation and football instincts, calling him one of the best leaders he has ever played alongside and praising his influence on Kansas City’s young defenders.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/sports/nfl/news/patrick-mahomes-gets-emotional-as-chiefs-legends-return-to-training-camp-and-reopen-old-memories/articleshow/133146424.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/sports/nfl/news/patrick-mahomes-gets-emotional-as-chiefs-legends-return-to-training-camp-and-reopen-old-memories/articleshow/133146424.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-11T18:02:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133146518,imgsize-1035022.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California woman refused to sell her home; developers built a 246-unit complex around it]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="